  "nl_text": "The database name is rschema_0363, and it contains four tables: Book, Reader, Reader_book_borrowing, and Reader_book_reservation. The Book table contains information about books, including their authors, available and circulating copies, ISBN, library location, price, publication date, publisher, shelf number, and title. The Reader table contains information about readers, including their addresses, ages, emails, genders, library card numbers, loan periods, maximum borrowing limits, names, phones, reader IDs, and reader types. The Reader_book_borrowing table contains information about book borrowings, including the actual return date, borrowing status, borrowing time, due date, ISBN, reader ID, and primary key (Reader_ID, ISBN, Borrowing_time). The Reader_book_reservation table contains information about book reservations, including the ISBN, reader ID, reservation expiration time, reservation status, reservation time, and primary key (Reader_ID, ISBN, Reservation_time). The foreign keys in the Reader_book_borrowing and Reader_book_reservation tables reference the primary keys in the Book and Reader tables, respectively.",
  "gold_question": "This is a library management system. For book management, the system maintains basic book information, including ISBN, title, author, publisher, publication date, price, number of copies available, number of copies in circulation, library location, and shelf number. For reader management, the system maintains reader information including reader ID, library card number, name, gender, age, phone, email, address, reader type, maximum borrowing limit, and loan period. For book borrowing management, the system records borrowing details including reader ID, ISBN, borrowing time, due date, actual return date, and borrowing status. For book reservation management, the system supports readers to reserve books, recording reader ID, ISBN, reservation time, reservation expiration time, and reservation status.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0363.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0363\nCREATE TABLE `book` (\n  `isbn` varchar(13) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `authors` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `publisher` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `publication_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `library_location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `shelf_number` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `available_copies` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `circulating_copies` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`isbn`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `reader` (\n  `reader_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `age` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) NOT NULL,\n  `library_card_number` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `loan_period` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `max_borrowing_limit` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `reader_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`reader_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `reader_book_borrowing` (\n  `reader_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `isbn` varchar(13) NOT NULL,\n  `borrowing_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `due_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `actual_return_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `borrowing_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`reader_id`, `isbn`, `borrowing_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `reader_book_borrowing_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`reader_id`) REFERENCES `reader` (`reader_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `reader_book_borrowing_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`isbn`) REFERENCES `book` (`isbn`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `reader_book_reservation` (\n  `reader_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `isbn` varchar(13) NOT NULL,\n  `reservation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `reservation_expiration_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `reservation_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`reader_id`, `isbn`, `reservation_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `reader_book_reservation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`reader_id`) REFERENCES `reader` (`reader_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `reader_book_reservation_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`isbn`) REFERENCES `book` (`isbn`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
